# Settings for the local module in zephyr/module.yml. All three are set in
# config/bb9900.conf; the defaults leave the ZMK fork's behaviour alone.

config BB9900_SCROLL_INVERT_X
    bool "Reverse horizontal trackpad scrolling"
    default n
    help
      Negate horizontal scroll deltas, so moving a finger left scrolls
      right. Vertical scrolling is unaffected unless
      BB9900_SCROLL_INVERT_Y is also set.

config BB9900_SCROLL_INVERT_Y
    bool "Reverse vertical trackpad scrolling"
    default n
    help
      Negate vertical scroll deltas, so moving a finger up scrolls down.
      Horizontal scrolling is unaffected unless
      BB9900_SCROLL_INVERT_X is also set.

config BB9900_SCROLL_AXIS_LOCK
    bool "Keep each scroll gesture on its starting axis"
    default n
    help
      Once scrolling starts, ignore the other axis until the trackpad has
      been still for a moment. A diagonal drag then scrolls on one axis
      instead of both. Vertical wins a tie and any diagonal that is not
      clearly horizontal, so slightly sloppy up/down drags stay vertical.
